      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 80677,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 941088,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "Flags & Offset Alignment",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "flow-mu42ugjw-10"
    },
    {
      "id": "sub-mu42ugjw-6-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -659,
      "y": 311,
      "width": 267,
      "height": 133,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42ugk0_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 119161,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 94266,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "IPv4 handles unequal link-layer\nMTUs along an end-to-end path\nthrough fragmentation. The 16-bit\nIdentification field pairs\nfragments from the same original\ndatagram, while Flags and Fragment\nOffset dictate order.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "edge-sub-mu42ugjw-6-sub-mu42ugjw-6-note",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-mu42ugjw-8-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -358,
      "y": 403,
      "width": 314,
      "height": 114,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42ugk0_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 826356,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 507096,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "When an outgoing packet exceeds the\negress link Maximum Transmission Unit\n(typically 1500 bytes for standard\nEthernet), the router verifies the Don't\nFragment (DF) flag before slicing\npayload into MTU-compliant segments.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "edge-flow-mu42ugjw-8-flow-mu42ugjw-8-note",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-mu42ugjw-10-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 19,
      "y": 403,
      "width": 314,
      "height": 114,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "grp_mu42ugk0_1"
      ],
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 585419,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 700956,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "text": "The router sets More Fragments (MF=1) on\nall slices except the last (MF=0). The\n13-bit Fragment Offset specifies the\nrelative payload position measured\nstrictly in 8-byte units to reconstruct\nthe original datagram.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "edge-flow-mu42ugjw-10-flow-mu42ugjw-10-note",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "diagram-mu42ugjw-12",
